  "description": "The same provider_message_id redelivered with a different body raises IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT and mutates nothing.",
  "why_it_exists": "Inbound delivery is at-least-once. Without a stored ingress fingerprint a redelivered message either appended a duplicate inbound row and a duplicate action, or - once a wall-clock value entered the fingerprint - a plain retry looked like a tampered message and raised a false IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT. The fingerprint is now derived only from the raw message, and every replay outcome is decided before the classifier runs. A message id is supplied by the provider and is not proof the content is the same; content substitution under a known id must reach a human. Covers suite cases X1, X1b, X1c.",
